  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "From the definition of $f(x),$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}(3a-2ax) \\\\  & =3a-2a(-2) \\\\  & =7a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-2,$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x) & =f(-2) \\\\ 7a & =14 \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
